{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-105308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-105308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}+8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-16{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 8 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-105308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01ff4f9c7cfbc1e6f7bf631451fd04cdf8eee3571cbdb957f1d1a47603f13441"} {"question" "q-105308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-105308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-105308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-105310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-105310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+15{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 15 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement III is false, while statements I and II are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-105310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01ff4f9c7cfbc1e6f7bf631451fd04cdf8eee3571cbdb957f1d1a47603f13441"} {"question" "q-105310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-105310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-105310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-155967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-155967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-155967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01ff4f9c7cfbc1e6f7bf631451fd04cdf8eee3571cbdb957f1d1a47603f13441"} {"question" "q-155967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-155967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-155967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-157236" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-157236" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-3+4 \\\\ 5-6+1 \\\\ 2-12+10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=-3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/s