capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-157256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =4[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/state.json" "file_sha256" "e898ce47f34f90927e061b2a19b905ad4a18ec06ce755ddbdacc001a4aaa48e1"} {"question" "q-157256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01ff4f9c7cfbc1e6f7bf631451fd04cdf8eee3571cbdb957f1d1a47603f13441"} {"question" "q-157256" "field" 